, "Incumbent Pat Ryan (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Pat Ryan, the Democratic incumbent, seeks another term in a Hudson Valley district that leans only slightly Democratic. He has raised about $5.4 million and holds $2.5 million on hand, while Republican Jacqueline Auringer has raised roughly $159,000 with about $22,000 available. Polling conducted by Democratic-leaning sponsors in July and September showed Ryan ahead by 14 to 17 points among likely voters, with a hypothetical matchup showing a narrower nine-point lead. Prediction markets on Kalshi and Polymarket both price Ryan's chances at about 96 percent.\n\nCampaign coverage has centered on debates, affordability, term limits, and attacks over Ryan's residency, but no independent polling or significant outside spending has emerged to suggest a competitive race. Incumbency, financial dominance, and market pricing all point to a comfortable Ryan win, with the district's modest Democratic lean reinforcing that picture.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.983, "margin": 17.1}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.971, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9767, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9844, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9723, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9684, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.971, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.978, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9814, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9828, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9869, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9867, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9709, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.972, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9706, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9758, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9805, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.